# PRE-EXISTING (48f82fb crashes the same way), not decision 48: a reference parameter whose default is a temporary built
# in another parameter's scope ("n Node&r = Node(7)"), with the default used at two call sites in different functions,
# crashes the code generator. The default is one operand shared by every call site (D8a); its constructor's instance
# scope (cgCtorHereArg -> cgWhereBuilt -> cgResolveScope) is a scope variable of the other call's function, which is
# not in this frame, so cgLookupVarAddr falls back to mangleGlobal with a NULL owner (codegen.c:252, mangleModPrefix).
#   expected: builds, prints "7 7"
#   actual:   "olang: internal compiler error: the compiler crashed (a segmentation fault)" (one call site builds fine)
type Node struct(v I64) {
    v
}
fn pickd(r Node&, n Node&r = Node(7)) Node&r { return n }
fn one(a Node&) I64 { return pickd(a).v }
fn main() ? {
    a Node& = Node(0)
    x := pickd(a)
    println($one(a) " " $x.v)
}
